  "intro": "Mr Karim brings Egyptian newspapers to class. A headline often puts the noun first and uses the present tense: الْوَزِيرُ يَفْتَتِحُ الْمِهْرَجَانَ (the minister opens the festival). The article below it starts with a past verb: اِفْتَتَحَ الْوَزِيرُ… (the minister opened…). In speeches and in the news you also hear إِنَّ (indeed). It starts a statement, and the noun after it ends in -a: إِنَّ الْأَخْبَارَ جَيِّدَة (the news is good).",
